Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
wait quentin tarantino almost made a  star trek movie and it was going to be  r-rated like pulp fiction in space  yes keep watching for the details about  what could have been  if quentin tarantino doesn't strike you  as the kind of director paramount would  have had on its shortlist for star trek  you'd be right the humble beginnings of  tarantino's never made sci-fi  blockbuster came from tarantino himself  not the studio tarantino is an admitted  fan of the franchise who has cited the  original series the city on the edge of  forever and the next generation episode  yesterday's enterprise as personal  favorites  one more ship will make no difference in  the here and now  but 22 years ago  one ship could have stopped this war  before it started it began with the 2015  interview with chris hardwick in which  tarantino discussed his love of trek and  his potential interest in helming a  movie hardwick initially asked the  director about star wars but tarantino  pivoted to say  i would be more inclined to do a star  trek kind of thing  in september 2017 tmz cornered tarantino  at an airport and questioned whether  he'd actually direct such a project he  responded it would be worth having a  meeting  by december of that year deadline  reported he was officially on board and  a rider's room was being assembled to  flesh out his pitch  things moved quickly and just a few  short weeks after the writer's room was  put together deadline reported that mark  l smith was announced as the writer of  the proposed film smith's previous work  which included the leonardo dicaprio  drama the revenant was a far cry from  the likes of previous track writers  roberto orsi and alex kurtzman mostly  known for pinning popcorn blockbusters  such as transformers and cowboys and  aliens  in an interview with bulletproof  screenwriting smith spoke about writing  the script with tarantino and working  with jj abrams production company bad  robot he said  they just called me it was like the day  later and said hey are you up for it you  want to go and if so then you know  quentin wants to wants to hook up so i  said yeah sure  he continued  and that was the first day i met quentin  in the room and he's reading a scene  that he wrote i told him i was so mad i  didn't record it on my phone it would be  so valuable it was amazing  smith gave a few hints about the still  unknown plot but mostly talked about his  enthusiasm about the project in a 2019  interview with empire magazine tarantino  himself noted that the script was done  as he weighed his options for his next  project saying  there's a script that exists for it now  i need to weigh in on it but i haven't  been able to do that yet  a year after the project's announcement  the film's story was still a tightly  guarded secret nobody knew who would  star but the biggest question on  everybody's lips was whether tarantino  himself would direct or just take  producer and story credits paramount  must have been hopeful he would take the  helm but many outlets were skeptical  mostly because tarantino wasn't known  for directing properties that he hadn't  created while he had directed a handful  of episodes for tv series including er  and csi his films were all originals  with the exception of jackie brown which  was an adaptation of an elmore leonard  novel two years into development  tarantino was still uncertain whether  he'd direct and the internet was abuzz  with rumors that he might be stepping  away deadline caught up with him and  asked him about the gossip he replied i  might be steering away from it but we'll  see i haven't completely decided or  talked to anyone involved nothing is  official in 2020 deadline reported  tarantino had officially dropped out and  that if the movie were to be made he  wouldn't be sitting in the director's  chair  tarantino's ninth film as director once  upon a time in hollywood hit theaters in  2019 and while that movie made quite a  splash his star trek proposal was still  a big topic speaking once again to  deadline the director revealed that his  trek would be a balance between classic  star trek and his own pulp fiction  tarantino also expressed his grievances  with trek actors who had tried to tamp  down the project he said their comments  weren't accurate because they weren't as  in the know as they claimed he named one  name specifically saying i get annoyed  at simon pegg he doesn't know anything  about what's going on and he keeps  making all these comments as if he knows  about stuff  one of the comments he said he's like  well look it's not going to be pulp  fiction in space yes it is it's at the  very least unique in that regard  it's an interesting point  come on let's get into character  one actor who didn't seem to upset  tarantino with his comments was carl  urban who played leonard bones mccoy in  the three j.j abrams produced star trek  films in a 2018 interview with  trekmovie.com the actor said he heard  the pitch and confirmed just how wild it  was he also confirmed rumors that the  film would carry an r rating a first for  the franchise  while some were concerned this meant the  film would be filled with cursing and  nudity urban noted that it was more  about showcasing the true horrors of  space explaining you shouldn't worry  that it's going to be full of obscenity  and stuff he wants an r rating to really  make those beats of consequence land it  allows some breath gives him some leeway  to do that according to deadline  tarantino himself had asked the studio  for an r rating with paramount and  production partner bad robot agreeing to  it the director later confirmed it in  his 2019 deadline interview saying if  you've seen my nine movies you kind of  know my way is an r rated way and a way  that is without certain restrictions  tarantino also said that producer j.j  abrams was fully on board and likened it  to recent r-rated blockbusters saying  deadpool showed that you can rethink  these things do them in a different way  so really even before jj knew what the  idea was his feeling was if it wants to  be an r rating fine if it wants to be  the wild bunch in space fine  without plot details many wondered if we  might see chris pine and zachary quinto  return especially given that the last  film in the series star trek beyond was  considered a disappointment some  wondered if there might be an all-new  cast but tarantino himself professed his  love for the abrams cast and it soon  became clear that if the film were to  move forward that cast would return in  the 2017 deadline interview tarantino  said  that's why i actually really was so  taken with jj abrams first reboot and  how fantastic i thought chris pine  channeled william shatner he's playing  the william shatner version of kirk and  he's doing a fantastic job at it i mean  perfect frankly and zachary quinto is  perfect as spock  in july 2018 quinto spoke to usa today  and confirmed his involvement alongside  the cast of the previous three films i'm  thrilled that we might have the  opportunity to work with him and see  what he would do with us in this  universe i've been a fan of his for  years and i'm really inspired by his  originality  in his interview with bulletproof  screenwriter mark l smith explained how  the story of the movie involved a cool  gangster scene a deadline report also  mentioned that it might be a 1930s  gangster story which immediately got  fans speculating that it could be  inspired by or related to the classic  original series episode a piece of the  action the 1968 episode of the original  star trek series saw kirk spock and  bones land on an alien planet with a  culture entirely based around  prohibition era chicago the planet had  apparently been visited by another  federation starship in the days before  the prime directive and that ship  unwittingly contaminated the culture by  leaving behind a book titled chicago  mobs of the 20s  though it may not be what benny expected  a star trek gangster film certainly fit  tarantino's description of something  we'd never seen in a big sci-fi movie  and there's no doubt it would have  offered him plenty of opportunities for  the kinds of crime stories he does best  following the release of star trek  beyond paramount was unsure of where to  take the franchise while audiences and  critics seem to like the film it  disappointed at the ticket counter  failing to live up to its predecessors  unsure of how to proceed paramount was  thrilled to hear of tarantino's interest  but the studio also decided not to put  all its eggs in one basket spock actor  zachary quinto told deadline there were  as many as three different scripts in  development before the sequel was  officially given the green light  i think there's a couple of scripts you  know because there was a  script being written before quentin  tarantino  quinto told et canada that a sequel  written by simon pegg and doug jung was  in the works before tarantino approached  the studio in 2017. noah holly of fargo  and legion was also reportedly  developing a screenplay that nearly went  into production screenwriters jd payne  and patrick mckay were also working on a  story that was dubbed star trek iv the  project was said to be directed by sj  clarkson and would have starred chris  hemsworth apparently entirely separate  from the version entering production in  2022 to be directed by matt jackman  rod roddenberry son of star trek creator  gene roddenberry was pretty vocal about  his displeasure with paramount bringing  in tarantino to helm a new trek film  roddenberry serves as an executive  producer on the many new star trek  series including discovery and strange  new worlds and he also acts as a steward  for the brand his father created in a  2021 interview with forbes he said he's  a fan of tarantino insisting that his  rejection of an r-rated tarantino trek  film had to do with the integrity of the  franchise he said  i struggle with the tarantino star trek  film because the way i'm pretty myopic  with the way i see star trek  i grew up with fans saying how star trek  inspired them and gave them hope for the  future it's the optimism and the  messaging in there that makes star trek  what it was  with that in mind roddenberry didn't  love the idea of pulp fiction and space  he continued i'll be honest that doesn't  work for me but he is a fan and i think  as a fan he probably understands to some  degree that star trek has to have some  of this hopeful optimistic  messaging many trek fans were excited  about the prospect of tarantino  producing something risky and daring one  user on trackmovie.com wrote tarantino  would bring something fresh and the  characters would be vibrant and logical  they added that the director's  involvement would reinvigorate the film  franchise others weren't as happy about  it another user declared that under no  circumstances should this be allowed to  happen  on reddit user dylan vincent seemed to  agree with rod roddenberry saying this  is such a bad idea the original spirit  of star trek gets no respect anymore  another redditor concho bear offered  another viewpoint saying i really hope  this happens this would be insane i love  trek and tarantino and they together  could be amazing with the idea  reportedly scrapped it seems the  naysayers got their way  as the rumor mills swirled about  tarantino's star trek project several  major star trek alumni expressed  interest in reprising their roles in an  interview with reuters william shatner  expressed his love for the director and  his passionate longing to return his  captain kirk he said  quentin tarantino said something in the  paper that somebody said to me that he  loved me and quentin i love you if  you're going to do star trek hey 50  years later a few pounds heavier come on  not a problem i'd like to do it george  takei who played sulu on the original  series told yahoo entertainment of his  interest but also said it would all  depend on the script  and it wasn't just original series stars  who spoke up patrick stewart who played  captain picard on star trek the next  generation made it clear that he'd love  to return if tarantino was involved  telling the hollywood reporter one of my  dreams is to work with tarantino i  admire his work so much and to be in a  tarantino film would give me so much  satisfaction so if he is going to direct  something to do with star trek i would  embrace it  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movie franchises are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one

